Here's a reproducible example with data.  Note how the R^2 value for y2 changes.  I think it has something to do with the 0* for the second predictor in mod2 - but the variance explained in the first response variable doesn't change, and hence the R^2 shouldn't change, so I fear there's a bug in here somewhere...

library(lavaan)

set.seed(2002)

adf <- data.frame(x=rnorm(100), x1 = rnorm(100), y1 = rnorm(100), y2 = rnorm(100))

mod1 <- '

y2 ~ x + x1 + y1

'

mod2 <- '

y2 ~ x + x1 + y1

y1 ~ x1 + 0*x

'

fit1 <- sem(mod1, adf)

fit2 <- sem(mod2, adf)

####

> inspect(fit1, "r2")

        y2

0.06541799

> inspect(fit2, "r2")

          y2           y1

0.0773845403 0.0003273043

